    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> regained its independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in March 1956 and from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> a month later, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-v-of-morocco">Mohammed V</a> became King in 1957; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaouite-dynasty">Alawi dynasty</a> that had seized power in 1631 still reigns.</li><li>Under Hassan II (1961–1999) a truth commission later confirmed nearly 10,000 cases of abuse, from death in detention to forced exile, in the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/years-of-lead-morocco">Years of Lead</a>'; in 1975 his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/green-march">Green March</a> sent 350,000 civilians into the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> has occupied ever since.</li><li>Mohammed VI answered the protests of 2011 with a new constitution, rejoined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-union">African Union</a> in 2017 and normalised relations with Israel in 2020 in exchange for American recognition of Moroccan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-sahara">Western Sahara</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> was the first nation to recognise the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Mohammed III placed American merchant ships under his protection on 20 December 1777, and the Moroccan–American Treaty of Friendship of 1786 is the United States' oldest unbroken friendship treaty.</p></aside>
    </section>

